Of course, you've ignored in this argument that these round screens
were in fact vector CRTs rather than raster CRTs.  To make *color*
vector CRTs is not at all easy.  (Have you tried to buy a copy of the
Tempest arcade game?  It had a color vector CRT, and very few have
survived.)  AFAIK, no machine that Nethack has been ported to has a
vector CRT commerically available without a (very?) custom order.  I'm
not even sure anyone is producing vector CRTs in mass quantities for
anything other than oscilloscopes, and many (most?) new o'scopes are
digital (and raster) now.  Always excepting radar displays, of course
(but many of those are raster now if you buy them new in the
US/Europe...)

